<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  M18, ATTLIST-default round. An ATTRIBUTE'S DEFAULT IS A USE OF WHATEVER IT IS
  BUILT FROM.

  `<!ATTLIST foo bar CDATA "&lt;&gt;&quot;">` says `bar`'s default value is
  assembled from `lt`, `gt` and `quot`, and an attribute cannot be given its
  default without expanding them. That claim was dropped: an EntityRef was only
  collected under an OWNING ELEMENT, and a DTD declaration has no element above it.
  This is the third instance of that same structural reason — after entity
  replacement text and parameter references — and the third time the answer has been
  "work out what the declaration is about, because nothing in the tree owns it".

  THE OWNER IS THE ATTRIBUTE, not the element the ATTLIST is about, and that is what
  makes the ruling derivable rather than a preference. The default is a property of
  `bar`, so `bar` is what depends on `lt`; and it is consistent with the
  `contains foo -> bar` edge the analyzer already publishes for the declaration
  itself. Attaching it to `foo` would claim `foo` has a dependency its own
  declaration does not mention.

  NINE of the ten corpus sites are the PREDEFINED entities, so they resolve as
  `builtin` — the same `&lt; &gt; &quot;` M18 settled — and the fixture has to
  assert that rather than assume it, because "an entity reference in a DTD is
  unresolved" is exactly the assumption being corrected.

  The last two cases are the ones that must NOT produce an edge:

    - `&ns;` inside a NAMESPACE URI. A URI is taken as a literal string; no
      processor expands entity references in it, which is the entire point of
      comparing an entity-expanded name against one. Publishing it would assert a
      dependency the language says does not exist — libxml2's
      `test/entity-in-ns-uri.xml` is a conformance probe for exactly this.
    - `%zz;` in a parameter-entity VALUE form, which names nothing.
-->
<!DOCTYPE root [
  <!ELEMENT root (#PCDATA)>
  <!ATTLIST root id ID #IMPLIED>
  <!ATTLIST root styled CDATA "&lt;b&gt; &quot;quoted&quot; &apos;q&apos;">
  <!ATTLIST root declared CDATA "&known;">
  <!ATTLIST root dangling CDATA "&neverDeclared;">
  <!ENTITY % zz '&#60;'>
  <!ENTITY known "a real declared entity">
  <!ENTITY ns "urn:x&#38;y">
]>
<root xmlns:one="urn:literal" xmlns:two="&ns;" id="a">text</root>